WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.020
Every living organism is
made of one or more cells.

2
00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:08.310
And new cells come only from
existing cells, by dividing.

3
00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:10.860
Most are far too small to see.

4
00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:15.230
A red blood cell is far smaller
than the finest mark on a ruler.

5
00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:19.870
So how can you measure the length of a
cell you can only see through a microscope?

6
00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:23.170
In this mission, you'll
work down a ladder of units,

7
00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:26.650
each step a thousand times
smaller than the last.

8
00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:30.270
Then you'll set up a slide of
cells and focus it properly:

9
00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:32.770
low power first, then high.

10
00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:37.480
Your mission: find out how to measure the
real length of a cell seen only through

11
00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:38.430
a microscope.
